# OpenSocrates for Codex

This package provides the Codex command-hook and skill boundary for
OpenSocrates {{PRODUCT_VERSION}}. Its authorized Codex-only prototype path
selects validated authored reasoning content for one user prompt; it does not
execute a user task, create a hosted service, or add telemetry. Prompts,
transcripts, local paths, tool input/output, credentials, and hidden reasoning
are not retained by the native adapter.

The package was generated from content revision {{CONTENT_REVISION}} with
semantic bundle identity `{{SEMANTIC_HASH}}` and {{METHOD_COUNT}} generated
method skill wrappers. These values are read from the canonical bundle at
build time; they are not host or manifest claims.

## Package and trust path

- Manifest: `.codex-plugin/plugin.json`
- Hook definition: `hooks/hooks.json`
- Fixed launcher: `{{PACKAGE_LAUNCHER_PATH}}`; this exact `bin/` placement is required and
  no root-level or PowerShell launcher is shipped.
- Native runtime: `runtime/<target>/opensocrates-runtime/`, resolved by
  the launcher relative to the plugin root
- Writable product data, when enabled by the host, is owned by the host's
  `PLUGIN_DATA` location; this package does not request a remote service.
- Complete selected reasoning content is written only to an owner-only OS
  temporary file for the active turn.

{{PACKAGE_RELEASE_BOUNDARY}}

Codex reviews local command hooks before execution. Review the exact hook
definition and approve the package only when its local files and fixed
launcher behavior are acceptable. A changed package or hook hash requires a
fresh review. Installation or skill resolution does not prove hook trust,
method activation, or public-artifact confirmation.

After installation, open one interactive Codex session and complete the
one-time interactive hook approval before relying on automatic selection.
Until then, non-interactive `codex exec` silently skips untrusted hooks. The
package and launcher are release-validated, but there is no live Codex
hook-delivery receipt for this release.

## Default v1.3 decision-point entry

The default runtime emits only bounded discovery guidance on user submission and
compact restoration. It selects no initial method, calls no selector model for
this entry, and does not create a method artifact that Stop would force an agent
to read after abandonment. The agent reads the installed controller and performs
in-turn decision lookup before each materially changed judgment. Used methods
still require complete canonical reads and their public grounding audit. The
new lookup has agent-reported availability, not native grounding receipts.

## Retained legacy selector lifecycle (not the v1.3 default)

The following describes the compatibility selector adapter available to existing
embedders. It is covered by regression tests, but is not the default decision-point
entry and its automatic-read claims must not be transferred to the new path.

This source contract does not establish a live Codex Desktop or CLI receipt.
The generated package configures `SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`,
`PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `PreCompact`, `Stop`, and `SessionEnd`, but only
`UserPromptSubmit` runs the selector. `SessionStart(source=compact)` may
re-emit a reference to an active file without starting another selector.
Other session-start, tool, compaction, Stop, and SessionEnd paths finish with
literal empty stdout.

For each `UserPromptSubmit`, the package starts one fresh ephemeral
`openai-codex` selector using the pinned local SDK/runtime and the user's
existing Codex OAuth/app-server session. It evaluates the current prompt
first, then may read transcript, workspace, transcript-referenced files, or
tool data only on demand and read-only as untrusted data. Set
`OPENSOCRATES_SELECTOR_TRANSCRIPT_ACCESS=0` to disable transcript access.
The selector does not use web access or persist raw prompt/context, OAuth,
selector reasoning, raw SDK data, or a selector trace.

The selector uses an isolated working directory and selector-only
instructions, a read-only sandbox, disabled hooks/plugins, and a separate
recursion marker. It omits an explicit model choice and uses the internal
medium-effort policy. A valid result is exactly one `additionalContext`
message containing teacher questions to settle, validated selected names, an
owner-only temporary Markdown path, and a requirement to read the complete
authored theory and examples before acting. The
30-second internal deadline cancels/closes without retry, progress, or error
output. Non-intervention and every failure, malformed result, unknown ID, or
invalid artifact write literal empty stdout with exit 0.

The temporary file contains authored OpenSocrates content only. `Stop` removes
the current turn directory immediately, `SessionEnd` removes the session
directory, and `SessionStart` sweeps files left by crashes after 24 hours.

The current 48 methods are initial selector content, not a permanent catalog
or selection-count cap. `unified_exec`, `WebSearch`, and other non-shell/non-
MCP paths remain outside complete observation; capability status stays unknown
or degraded without a dated native receipt.

## Capability and status

The fixed control boundary below is invoked only by the host integration after
the host trust flow. It is not a command for a model or user to run directly:

`${PLUGIN_ROOT}/bin/launch.sh control codex`

Direct shell execution has no host-issued typed stdin payload and therefore
cannot establish a native receipt.

Without a dated exact native receipt, capability status remains unknown or
documented degraded. Disabled hooks, untrusted hooks, and managed-only policy
excluding plugin hooks degrade honestly to skills-only Tier C. The prototype
does not turn installation, a manifest, or a synthetic fixture into a host
trust, quality, or uplift claim.

Generated source identity: `{{SOURCE_TREE_HASH}}`.

## Decision-point retrieval (v{{PRODUCT_VERSION}})

The controller links `skills/opensocrates/references/decision/guide.en.md` and `skills/opensocrates/references/decision/guide.ko.md`.
Read routing metadata and complete selected locale-specific canonical references
at a materially changed judgment within the same request. Mechanical steps need
none. This is agent-directed in-turn lookup, not automatic observation of every
reasoning transition. A delivered reference or agent read assertion is not proof
of application or better output. No prompt, transcript or reasoning state is
persisted by this path. Existing native hook/fallback boundaries remain in force.

The native `bin/launch.sh decision codex` command accepts one closed JSON
request on stdin. This is separate from host-only `control`; see
`skills/opensocrates/references/decision/request.json`. The standalone runtime also accepts `decision --stream`
for a volatile NDJSON session. No active host installation is needed for file lookup.

## Windows candidate

The Windows x64 archive uses `node bin/launch.mjs` and a bundled `.exe`. Node.js 20+ is required; Python and a Unix shell are not required for method retrieval. See the repository Windows support guide for the current validation boundary. Legacy SDK context/credential-copy selection is unavailable on Windows; decision-point retrieval is the supported path. Scheduled updates are unavailable; use a manual installer update.
